<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1991</h1><p class="ref-lede">1991 in world history: 38 events, 13 deaths, 1 work, 12 states founded and 17 that came to an end. 207 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1987">1987</a><a href="/years/1988">1988</a><a href="/years/1989">1989</a><a href="/years/1990">1990</a><a href="/years/1991" aria-current="page">1991</a><a href="/years/1992">1992</a><a href="/years/1993">1993</a><a href="/years/1994">1994</a><a href="/years/1995">1995</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-13">13 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet troops storm the Vilnius television tower</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces attacked unarmed crowds defending Lithuanian broadcasting sites in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>, killing 14 civilians. The violence strengthened support for Baltic independence at home and abroad.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-17">17 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Operation Desert Storm opens with air strikes on Iraq</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A US-led coalition began a massive air campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, which had occupied Kuwait since August 1990. A ground offensive in late February expelled Iraqi forces within 100 hours.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-28">28 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Gulf War ceasefire takes effect</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">One hundred hours after the ground offensive began, coalition forces halted operations, Kuwait having been liberated. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a> remained in power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-3">3 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rodney King's beating by Los Angeles police is filmed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A bystander videotaped officers beating Rodney King after a car chase. The officers' acquittal in April 1992 sparked riots in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> in which more than 60 people died.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-29">29 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Cyclone strikes the coast of Bangladesh</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A severe tropical cyclone drove a storm surge of up to six metres onto the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chittagong">Chittagong</a> coast, killing some 138,000 people. It led to wider investment in cyclone shelters and warnings.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-21">21 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rajiv Gandhi is assassinated in Tamil Nadu</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A suicide bomber from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liberation-tigers-of-tamil-eelam">Tamil Tigers</a> killed the former Indian prime minister at an election rally in Sriperumbudur. His mother, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a>, had been assassinated in 1984.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-15">15 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mount Pinatubo erupts in the Philippines</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The second-largest eruption of the twentieth century sent ash 35 km into the sky. Its aerosols cooled global temperatures by about 0.5°C, and timely evacuations saved thousands of lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-20">20 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bundestag votes to move Germany's government to Berlin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By 338 votes to 320, the parliament of reunified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a> as the seat of government. The move was completed in 1999.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-25">25 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Croatia and Slovenia declare independence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The two republics broke away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> on the same day. A brief war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a> was followed by much longer conflicts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-6">6 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tim Berners-Lee makes the World Wide Web public</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Tim Berners-Lee posted a summary of his World Wide Web project to an internet newsgroup, inviting outside collaboration. The web, created at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cern">CERN</a>, spread rapidly and transformed communication.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-19">19 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet hardliners launch a coup against Gorbachev</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Communist hardliners placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a> under house arrest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> and declared a state of emergency. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a> led resistance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, the coup collapsed, and the USSR dissolved by December.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-19">19 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hikers find Ötzi the Iceman in the Alps</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Two German hikers found a body in the ice on the Austrian-Italian border. Ötzi proved to be a man who died some 5,300 years ago, killed by an arrow, with his clothes and tools preserved.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-4">4 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pan Am ceases operations</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Pan American World Airways flew its last flight after 64 years. The airline had pioneered transoceanic air travel and launched the Boeing 747, but it never recovered from deregulation, recession and the Lockerbie bombing.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-8">8 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Leaders of Russia, Ukraine and Belarus agree to dissolve the USSR</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in the Belovezha Forest, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonid-kravchuk">Leonid Kravchuk</a> and Stanislav Shushkevich declared that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> had ceased to exist and created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-independent-states">Commonwealth of Independent States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-16">16 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Kazakhstan declares independence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Kazakhstan became the last Soviet republic to declare independence, days before the USSR was dissolved. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nursultan-nazarbayev">Nursultan Nazarbayev</a> led the vast Central Asian country for nearly three decades.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-25">25 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mikhail Gorbachev resigns as Soviet president</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In a televised address, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a> resigned. That evening the Soviet flag was lowered from the Kremlin and replaced by the Russian tricolour.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-31">31 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The last Soviet institutions cease to function</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By the end of the year, all remaining institutions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> had ceased to operate, days after Gorbachev's resignation. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715">Fifteen</a> independent states took its place.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/belovezha-accords" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belovezha-accords.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/belovezha-accords">Belovezha Accords</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Belovezha Accords were signed on 8 December 1991 at Viskuli in the Belovezha Forest of Belarus by the leaders of Russia, Ukraine and Belarus: Boris Yeltsin, Leonid Kravchuk and Stanislav Shushkevich.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/santa-cruz-massacre" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-cruz-massacre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/santa-cruz-massacre">Santa Cruz massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Santa Cruz massacre took place on 12 November 1991, when Indonesian troops opened fire on mourners and pro-independence demonstrators at the Santa Cruz cemetery in Dili, East Timor.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-agreements">Paris Peace Agreements</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Paris Peace Agreements were signed on 23 October 1991 by Cambodia's Supreme National Council, representing the rival factions, and eighteen other states to end the war in Cambodia that followed Vietnam's invasion of 1978.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/dissolution-of-the-soviet-union">Dissolution of the Soviet Union</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The dissolution of the Soviet Union was the breakup of the USSR into fifteen independent states in 1991.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-asuncion">Treaty of Asunción</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Asunción was signed on 26 March 1991 by Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay and Uruguay in the Paraguayan capital.</p></div></li></ol></section>
